  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oracle Health Government Services obligated $1.6B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Oracle Health Government Services won 29 awards so far, with an average award size of $54.6M. Oracle Health Government Services obligations are up 57.2% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date period. Oracle Health Government Services has a multi-year pattern of obligations that ranged from $971M in FY21 to $2B in FY22 and then moved through $825M in FY23, $893M in FY24, and $1B in FY25 before reaching $1.6B in FY26. Oracle Health Government Services receives its FY2026 obligations primarily from the Department of Veterans Affairs, which accounts for $1.6B of buying agency activity. Oracle Health Government Services sells mostly in Computer Systems Design Services, where obligations total $1.6B, with smaller activity in Computer Facilities Management Services at $3.6M and Used Household and Office Goods Moving at $110K. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
